# sriq: an INVERSE decides a subsumption. A ⊑ ∃r.B and B ⊑ ∀r⁻.C give A ⊑ C:
# A's r-successor is in B, and B sends whatever is r-related to it into C.
# Read r for r⁻ and the subsumption is lost.
# Expect: A ⊑ C.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] .
:B rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty [ owl:inverseOf :r ] ; owl:allValuesFrom :C ] .
